cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use duelswarm in research, please cite it as below."
title: "duelswarm — a sandboxed cyber range for studying adaptive AI attackers and defenders against a fixed rule enforcer"
authors:
  - family-names: "Cano"
    given-names: "Dante"
    email: "drcano@ucsd.edu"
    affiliation: "University of California, San Diego"
repository-code: "https://github.com/drcano/duelswarm"
url: "https://github.com/drcano/duelswarm"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "AI safety"
  - "cybersecurity"
  - "adversarial co-evolution"
  - "pre-registered research"
  - "authorization enforcement"
abstract: >
  duelswarm is a sandboxed cyber range in which two adaptive LLM agents (a red attacker and a blue
  defender) run as co-evolving populations against a non-adaptive authorization enforcer and a
  tamper-evident hash-chained log. The range exists to test four pre-registered falsifiable claims
  about what a fixed rule enforcer does to a reflexively adapting adversary while a monitor sitting
  at the same interface erodes against the same adversary. Every result is cold-re-derivable from
  the raw chain by a party trusting neither agent.
